    /// <summary>A navigation pane with menu items and a content area (WinUI's `NavigationView`). The pane is at the left (`Left`, `LeftCompact`, `LeftMinimal`, or chosen by the width in `Auto`: the display modes `Expanded`, `Compact` and `Minimal`) or at the top (`Top`). The template of the WinUI theme is WinUI's (`NavigationView.xaml`): the control finds WinUI's parts (`RootSplitView`, `TogglePaneButton`, `NavigationViewBackButton`, `NavigationViewCloseButton`, `PaneAutoSuggestButton`, `PaneTitleTextBlock`, `PaneTitleHolder`, `PaneTitlePresenter`, `PaneTitleOnTopPane`, `MenuItemsHost`, `FooterMenuItemsHost`, `TopNavMenuItemsHost`, `TopFooterMenuItemsHost`, the content controls of the pane header, custom content, footer and auto suggest box of the left and the top pane, `ContentLeftPadding`), sets their contents and the values of [`template_settings`](Self::template_settings) as WinUI's code does, and sets WinUI's visual states as pseudo-classes (`:compact`, `:expanded`, `:minimal`, `:top-navigation-minimal`, `:minimal-with-back-button`, `:toggle-pane-button-visible`, `:header-collapsed`, `:auto-suggest-box-collapsed`, `:closed-compact`, `:list-size-compact`, `:pane-not-overlaying`, `:back-button-collapsed`, `:pane-collapsed`, and `:back-button-row-visible` for the row WinUI sizes in code). The Fluent and Simple themes have no template. The menu items are realized in stack panels, not in `ItemsRepeater`s with a hierarchical `SelectionModel` (follow-up F1). Missing (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 10.4): the overflow of the top pane, the animations of the pane, the shadow of the pane, the padding of the title bar, the shoulder navigation and the selectors of templates and styles.</summary>
