    /// <summary>A control to move through the pages of a paged content (WinUI's `PagerControl`): buttons to the first, previous, next and last page around a combo box of the page numbers, a number box to type one, or a button for each page (`DisplayMode`). `NumberOfPages` is -1 while the number of pages is not known; `SelectedPageIndex` is the index of the page, from 0, kept in the range of the pages, and its changes raise `SelectedIndexChanged`. The template is the control theme of the WinUI theme (`Controls/PagerControl.xaml`, from WinUI's `PagerControl.xaml`), with WinUI's parts `FirstPageButton`, `PreviousPageButton`, `NextPageButton`, `LastPageButton`, `ComboBoxDisplay`, `NumberBoxDisplay`, `NumberPanelItemsRepeater` and `NumberPanelCurrentPageIndicator`. The control sets WinUI's visual states as pseudo-classes: `:numberbox`, `:combobox` and `:numberpanel` (the display mode), `:infinite` (InfiniteItems), and for each button `:&lt;button&gt;collapsed`, `:&lt;button&gt;hidden` and `:&lt;button&gt;disabled` (`:firstcollapsed`, `:nexthidden`, ...). The Fluent and Simple themes have no template for it (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 5.1). Differences (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, G2): the number panel is an items control whose panel is a horizontal stack panel, where WinUI has an `ItemsRepeater` with a `StackLayout` (`ferroui-controls` cannot depend on the repeater crate); the indicator of the current page moves without WinUI's `RepositionThemeTransition`.</summary>
    public interface IPagerControl : ITemplatedControl { }

