    /// <summary>A group of radio buttons with one selection (WinUI's `RadioButtons`). The items are shown as [`RadioButton`]s: an item that is a radio button is its own container, and another item is the content of a radio button. The selection is the selection of the items control (`SelectedIndex`, `SelectedItem`, `SelectionChanged`), kept with the checked state of the containers. The arrow keys move the focus and the selection within the group without wrapping, Tab enters the group at the selected button, and Ctrl with an arrow key moves the focus only. The template is the control theme of the WinUI theme (`Controls/RadioButtons.xaml`, from WinUI's `RadioButtons.xaml`), with the parts `PART_HeaderPresenter` and `PART_ItemsPresenter` (WinUI's `HeaderContentPresenter` and the `ItemsRepeater` `InnerRepeater`); the theme sets the items panel, a [`RadioButtonsPanel`](crate::primitives::RadioButtonsPanel) with the spacing of the resources `RadioButtonsColumnSpacing` and `RadioButtonsRowSpacing`. The Fluent and Simple themes have no template for it (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 5.1). The exclusive check is the radio button group manager's: the containers are the logical children of the group and have no group name, so checking one unchecks the others. The group itself only checks the container of a new selection, and unchecks the container of the old one when no container is checked instead (a cleared selection, or one whose container is not realized), which the group manager never does (WinUI's `Select` writes both containers). Missing (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, Input): WinUI's element factories and `DataTemplateSelector` as `ItemTemplate`.</summary>
