    /// <summary>The shadow of the theme (WinUI `Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Media.ThemeShadow`): set as the `Shadow` of an element, the element casts the shadow of its elevation, the Z of its `Translation`, as the controls of WinUI do under their popups (32 for a flyout, 16 for a tool tip, 128 for a content dialog). WinUI 3 draws every theme shadow as a drop shadow ([`is_drop_shadow_mode`](Self::is_drop_shadow_mode)): an ambient and a directional shadow around the element, the darker in the dark theme, none in a high contrast theme. A `ThemeShadow` can be shared by several elements; it has no appearance of its own. [`receivers`](Self::receivers) are the elements the projected shadows of WinUI (the root and the open popups by default) would fall on. WinUI 3 keeps the collection and its validation but does not draw projected shadows, so the receivers do not change the drawing here either.</summary>
